visit|go-and-spend-time|VERB|go somewhere to spend time|To go to a person or place in order to spend time there.|đến thăm; ghé thăm|We visited the local museum during the school break.|Chúng tôi đến thăm bảo tàng địa phương trong kỳ nghỉ học.|Transitive visit a place or person; a visit to uses to in the noun construction.|0
visit|occasion-of-visiting|NOUN|occasion spent at a place or with someone|An occasion when someone goes to a person or place and spends time there.|chuyến thăm; lần ghé thăm|Her first visit to the island lasted a week.|Chuyến thăm hòn đảo đầu tiên của cô ấy kéo dài một tuần.|Countable; pay a visit to someone or somewhere describes making such a visit.|1
zero|number|NUMBER|no amount in counting|The number representing no amount, or the point from which a scale is measured.|không; số không|The display showed zero messages in the inbox.|Màn hình hiển thị không có tin nhắn nào trong hộp thư đến.|Before a count noun or used alone as a number; zero messages is plural despite the absence of messages.|0
cold|low-temperature|ADJECTIVE|having a low temperature|Having a low temperature, or feeling a lack of warmth.|lạnh|The cold floor made us look for our slippers.|Sàn nhà lạnh khiến chúng tôi tìm dép đi trong nhà.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; feel cold describes a person's sensation.|0
cold|common-illness|NOUN|minor respiratory illness|A common illness often involving a runny or blocked nose and a sore throat.|cảm lạnh|He stayed home because he had a cold.|Anh ấy ở nhà vì bị cảm lạnh.|Countable; have or catch a cold. This noun is distinct from cold weather.|1
grace|smooth-movement|NOUN|smooth and controlled movement|An attractive smoothness and control in the way someone moves.|sự duyên dáng; vẻ thanh thoát|The dancer crossed the stage with effortless grace.|Vũ công bước ngang sân khấu với vẻ thanh thoát tự nhiên.|Uncountable; with grace describes the quality of movement, not an individual step.|0
grace|courteous-conduct|NOUN|kind and composed behaviour|Kind, courteous, and composed behaviour towards others, especially in a difficult situation.|sự nhã nhặn; sự điềm đạm|She accepted the disappointing result with grace.|Cô ấy đón nhận kết quả đáng thất vọng một cách điềm đạm.|Uncountable in with grace; concerns manner of conduct rather than physical movement.|1
inferior|lower-rank-person|NOUN|person in a lower rank|A person regarded as having a lower rank or position than another person.|người ở cấp thấp hơn; cấp dưới|The officer refused to speak harshly to his inferiors.|Viên sĩ quan không chịu nói năng gay gắt với những người cấp dưới.|Countable and often disapproving or hierarchical; the term describes rank in this sense, not human worth.|-
